Running #VSLAM in a #vineyard with a learned place recognition backend: the #BLT dataset and #MegaLoc

🎬 Video: [VIDEO_LINK]
🔗 VSLAM-LAB: https://lnkd.in/gGZifSb3
🔗 AllFeature-VSLAM: https://lnkd.in/gRztKMHT
🔗 MegaLoc: https://github.com/gmberton/megaloc
🔗 BLT dataset: https://lcas.lincoln.ac.uk/wp/research/data-sets-software/blt/

The BACCHUS Long-Term (BLT) dataset comes from the Lincoln Centre for Autonomous Systems. A Thorvald II robot drives the same 500 m topological path through the Ktima Gerovassiliou vineyard in Epanomi, Greece, again and again across the whole 2022 growing season: eleven sessions from bare vines in March to full canopy in September. Front ZED2 RGB-D imagery, RTK-GNSS ground truth, and a robot deployed autonomously so every session follows the same route.
📄 https://doi.org/10.1002/rob.22228

Place recognition in AllFeature-VSLAM. The Bag-of-Words vocabulary is gone: loop and relocalisation candidates now come from MegaLoc, running natively inside the C++ pipeline as an ONNX model.

⏱️ At 5:00 in the video you can see the loop closure and the full graph correction that follows it. Watch the kernel of the graph as the robot revisits its earlier trajectory: the characteristic diagonal lines appear, parallel to the main diagonal.

